{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa Starts Dating Marco"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Dear Diary"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 9}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling aspects related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling aspects related to this level. Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling aspects related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling aspects related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling aspects related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le09ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Past Tense and Past Continuous Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Past Continuous tense to talk about something that was happening at a particular time in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You often use the Past Continuous tense together with the Simple Past tense. </br></br>The Past Continuous talks about a longer \u2018background' action."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The Simple Past talks about talks about a shorter event that happened in the middle of, or interrupted, the longer event."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the words <span class=\"strong\">when</span> and <span class=\"strong\">while</span> before the longer action."}, {"type": "example", "content": "While I was admiring his lamp, I found out he has a sister named Francesca."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Things were going so well. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "He grabbed some ice-cream from a street vendor."}, {"type": "example", "content": "He invited me over to his apartment."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to stumble"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to hit your foot on something when you are walking or running so that you fall or almost fall"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Marco stumbled in the movie theatre and spilled popcorn all over Vanessa."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob08aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you write when you are reflecting on a date."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bottled up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be filled with emotion but unable to express it"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Vanessa has so many bottled up emotions."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob08aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "taste"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the ability to choose what is appealing, attractive, appropriate, or enjoyable"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Marco has great taste in furniture."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob08aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "make this up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to improve a situation in the future"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He better make this up to me."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob08aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to reflect"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to think carefully about something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I wanted to reflect on Marco's behavior."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob08aud05"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write an 80-100 word diary entry about an event in your life."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Include the Simple Past tense and Past Continuous tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Include information on people, events and places."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use informal words and phrases."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your diary entry aloud to a partner or family member."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write a diary entry about an event in my life."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I include information about people, places and events."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use informal words and phrases."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my diary entry aloud to a partner or family member."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le09ob08re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le09ob08re2img06.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn5le09ob08re2img06.jpg"}, {"text": "Dear Diary,</br></br>I have so many emotions bottled up inside. Marco is amazing in so many ways. We went to the movies last week to see, <span class=\"italic\">Dinner at Mickey's</span>.  I have never laughed so hard in my life.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn5le09ob08re2img06.jpg"}, {"text": "I wasn't laughing though when Marco stumbled up the stairs and spilt popcorn all over me! We grabbed some ice-cream from a street vendor and Marco invited me over to his apartment. He showed me his great taste in furniture and accessories. While I was admiring his lamp, I found out he has a sister named Francesca.", "id": 2, "time": "16500", "image": "engenn5le09ob08re2img06.jpg"}, {"text": "Things were going so well until Marco started making fun of me.  He found it hilarious that I thought he painted a Picasso. I was so annoyed and a little embarrassed. He's so annoying! He better make this up to me.</br></br>Vanessa", "id": 3, "time": "39700", "image": "engenn5le09ob08re2img06.jpg"}]}}]}, {"id": 2, "type": "video", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"ty